 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“I was eleven years of age, and my sisters Rachel and Susannah were older. We all heard the alarm, and were up and ready to help fit out father and brother, who made an early start for Concord. We were set to work making <i>cartridges</i> and assisting mother in cooking for the army. We sent off a large quantity of food for the soldiers, who had left home so early that they had but little breakfast. We were frightened by hearing the noise of guns at Concord; our home was near the river, and the sound was conducted by the water.</p>\n<p>I suppose it was a dreadful day in our home, and sad indeed; for our brother, so dearly loved, never came home.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Alice Stearns Abbott, Citizen of Bedford, Massachusetts, on the Beginning of Fighting Concord, 1775</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614939,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In the excerpt provided, the violent conflict described in 1775 most directly contributed to which of the following events?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167728,
     "content_html": "Colonial governments writing a petition for peace, with a diplomatic solution to conclude the bloodshed"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167727,
     "content_html": "Immediate Colonial call to arms and declaration of war against the British"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167729,
     "content_html": "Calls for military and political action, which resulted in the meeting of the Second Continental Congress"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167726,
     "content_html": "An alliance with the French, who would provide needed financial and military support"
    }
   ],
